"""Regenerate native display strings from the launcher's embedded catalog."""
from pathlib import Path
import runpy,json
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]
rows=runpy.run_path(str(root/'launcher/bbport_integrated_localization.py'))['TRANSLATIONS']
quote=lambda text:json.dumps(text,ensure_ascii=False)
text='''// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
// Generated by generate_language_text.py from the launcher's shared catalog.
#pragma once
#include <string_view>
namespace PcLanguage {
enum class Language { English,Spanish,Russian,Japanese,French,German,Italian,Portuguese };
inline Language Detect(const char16_t* title){
 if(!title)return Language::English;
 const std::u16string_view value(title);
'''
for i,label in enumerate(rows['Key Bindings']):text+=f' if(value==u{quote(label)})return Language({i});\n'
text+=' return Language::English;\n}\ninline const char* Translate(const char* source,Language language){\n if(!source||language==Language::English)return source;\n struct Row{const char* en;const char* translated[7];};\n static constexpr Row rows[]={\n'
for row in rows.values():text+='{'+quote(row[0])+', {'+','.join(quote(v) for v in row[1:])+'}},\n'
text+=' };\n for(const auto& row:rows)if(std::string_view(source)==row.en)return row.translated[int(language)-1];\n return source;\n}\ninline const char* Translate(const char* source,bool spanish){return Translate(source,spanish?Language::Spanish:Language::English);}\n}\n'
Path(__file__).with_name('language_text.h').write_text(text)
